-- The protective statutes' root (MMS-601): the statutes that set a floor an
-- agreement, a circular and the takanon cannot go below — the Minimum Wage
-- Law, the Wage Protection Law and the Severance Pay Law
-- (l4/laws/*.l4) — and the floor each sets for an item of the shared
-- vocabulary (l4/lib/vocabulary.l4), for a case. It is a `collection root`
-- (l4/lib/precedence.l4), but not one of the collections the root sets
-- against each other: its ruling is weighed last, over whichever
-- instrument their precedence left governing, by the Collective
-- Agreements Law's §21 (`the ruling under the statutes' floor`).
--
-- No item of the vocabulary is yet one of these statutes' floors: the
-- minimum wage is a floor on the pay its §3 counts, not on any one item,
-- and severance and deductions are not monthly items. So this root's
-- claims are empty for every item, and the floors are weighed in the
-- instruments' own files (the September 2016 agreement's top-up, the 2023
-- framework's hourly floor, circular תשע"ג/10's reduction, the completion
-- agreement's §93, the takanon's §1.28.2.3); a new item a statute floors
-- is a new branch of `the statutes' claims on`, and the statute's module
-- (l4/laws/) is imported here then — not before, since the root, and the
-- calculator that ships everything it reaches, would load it for nothing.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT precedence

§ `שורש החוקים המגינים — הרצפה שחוק קובע`

§§ `המסמכים`

-- Each statute as an instrument. A statute is `a provision of law`, which
-- the takanon's introduction lets prevail whatever its date, and which §21
-- puts above every agreement; so its date is never weighed, and the day
-- here is the first of its year (the day of its passing is not pinned).
`the Minimum Wage Law` MEANS
    `instrument` WITH
        `module`        IS "minimum-wage-law"
        `title`         IS "חוק שכר מינימום, התשמ\"ז-1987"
        `kind`          IS `a provision of law`
        `is the takanon` IS FALSE
        `issued`        IS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1987
        `practised for all state employees` IS TRUE
        `approved by the Finance Minister`  IS FALSE

`the Wage Protection Law` MEANS
    `instrument` WITH
        `module`        IS "wage-protection-law"
        `title`         IS "חוק הגנת השכר, התשי\"ח-1958"
        `kind`          IS `a provision of law`
        `is the takanon` IS FALSE
        `issued`        IS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1958
        `practised for all state employees` IS TRUE
        `approved by the Finance Minister`  IS FALSE

`the Severance Pay Law` MEANS
    `instrument` WITH
        `module`        IS "severance-pay-law"
        `title`         IS "חוק פיצויי פיטורים, התשכ\"ג-1963"
        `kind`          IS `a provision of law`
        `is the takanon` IS FALSE
        `issued`        IS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1963
        `practised for all state employees` IS TRUE
        `approved by the Finance Minister`  IS FALSE

`the protective statutes` MEANS
    LIST `the Minimum Wage Law`, `the Wage Protection Law`, `the Severance Pay Law`

§§ `הרצפה, לפי פריט`

-- What floor each statute sets for an item and a case. None of the items
-- of the vocabulary is one yet (above).
GIVEN i IS A `pay item`, c IS A `teaching case`
GIVETH A LIST OF `claim`
DECIDE `the statutes' claims on` i c IS
    EMPTY

§§ `הכרעת החוקים`

-- Of two statutes that floor one item, the employee has the higher floor:
-- each adds to the other as to an agreement (Minimum Wage Law §11,
-- Severance Pay Law §31).
GIVEN a IS A `claim`, b IS A `claim`
GIVETH A `claim`
DECIDE `the higher floor of` a b IS
    IF b's `answer` GREATER THAN a's `answer` THEN b ELSE a

GIVEN claims IS A LIST OF `claim`
GIVETH A MAYBE `ruling`
DECIDE `the statutes' floor among` claims IS
    CONSIDER claims
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN c FOLLOWED BY cs THEN
        JUST (`the ruling for` (foldl `the higher floor of` c cs) `the only instrument that speaks`)

`the statutes' root` MEANS
    `collection root` WITH
        `the collection`  IS "החוקים המגינים"
        `its instruments` IS `the protective statutes`
        `what each says`  IS `the statutes' claims on`
        `its ruling`      IS (GIVEN i, c YIELD `the statutes' floor among` (`the statutes' claims on` i c))
